{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789893803,"nonce":"1UOxtynladqxvk+vPj/wbm6NeF8=","title":"Interpreter: unsigned compare, division and shift ran as signed","message":"The ground tier lowered Binary on U8/U16/U32/U64/USize to the same ops as the signed types, so math.ult(-1, 2) was true, u64 division and remainder went through i64, and a logical shift right filled with the sign. Cranelift and LLVM were right, which hid it until main's tiering ran bodies without loops in the interpreter. Fixed in 39c9638 with UCmpLt/Le/Gt/Ge, UDiv, URem and UShr chosen by the instruction's type.","files":null}]}